WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.066 --> 01:08.651
-[birds cawing]
-[tense music plays]

01:10.445 --> 01:14.949
Would you like to come with me
to the moment of your death?

01:19.287 --> 01:20.288
Why would I go with you?

01:22.665 --> 01:25.460
I followed the Lord's orders
and bowed before the first human.

01:26.044 --> 01:28.379
Iblis and I have been brothers
for a long time,

01:28.463 --> 01:30.256
as well as each other's oldest enemies.

01:32.175 --> 01:34.219
Now he wants to kill you, Ki Ka-young.

01:34.803 --> 01:36.221
Your enemy's enemy…

01:38.431 --> 01:39.891
has to be an ally, no?

01:39.974 --> 01:41.601
[tense music continues]

01:56.825 --> 01:57.826
Get lost.

01:58.618 --> 01:59.452
Why?

01:59.536 --> 02:02.622
I don't believe your lies.
Your face betrays you.

02:03.873 --> 02:05.500
-Whoa!
-You okay?

02:05.583 --> 02:07.168
Did you bite your tongue or something?

02:08.002 --> 02:10.421
I felt somebody just beat up my master.

02:10.505 --> 02:13.133
Oh, really? Your master's getting beat up?

02:13.716 --> 02:14.926
Only two people would do that.

02:17.053 --> 02:19.722
[yelling]

02:19.806 --> 02:22.267
One of them is occupied, so that leaves…

02:22.350 --> 02:23.476
[screaming]

02:24.602 --> 02:27.397
Uh, I gotta get going now. Early morning.

02:31.526 --> 02:32.944
Morning, Ms. Ki.

02:34.445 --> 02:35.947
Everything all right?

02:36.030 --> 02:38.158
Hello. We're the police.

02:38.825 --> 02:40.910
Oh, gosh.
Did Ejllael report you for punching him?

02:40.994 --> 02:42.662
He just had to get the police involved.

02:42.745 --> 02:45.290
You're the one reporting me at the moment.

02:46.749 --> 02:49.169
-There's a missing person.
-Ah.

02:49.252 --> 02:53.590
Uh, yes. Do you happen to know this woman?
This village was her last known location.

02:54.090 --> 02:55.842
[sniffing]

02:56.426 --> 02:58.469
I usually use my nose
to find people. [sniffs]

02:58.553 --> 02:59.387
[grunts]

03:00.722 --> 03:01.973
We haven't seen her.

03:02.056 --> 03:04.183
Would it be okay
to take a picture of that?

03:04.267 --> 03:07.478
Of course. If you see anything at all
or remember something,

03:07.562 --> 03:08.605
please give us a call.

03:10.899 --> 03:11.733
[camera clicks]

03:16.362 --> 03:19.616
[suspenseful music plays]

03:37.842 --> 03:39.010
BLACK HAIR DYE

03:39.594 --> 03:40.428
[knocking]

03:42.388 --> 03:44.724
That's very strange. I was here last week.

03:45.308 --> 03:47.227
But why would they plan
another visit so soon?

03:49.646 --> 03:53.024
Anyone there? Ms. Shin Suk-ja?
It's your water filter tech.

03:54.651 --> 03:56.819
Whoa, so gross.
What's that horrible smell?

03:56.903 --> 03:59.948
-[siren wails]
-[people murmuring]

04:04.619 --> 04:07.538
Why do you always have
to overcomplicate things this way?

04:09.332 --> 04:11.834
If I'm to escort those
who die bravely but alone,

04:11.918 --> 04:13.878
I have to follow their playbook on death.

04:14.462 --> 04:16.798
I even filed the reports myself
until 40 years ago.

04:17.882 --> 04:19.175
I was way busier back then.

04:19.676 --> 04:21.427
I had to receive the complaints
of the dead,

04:21.511 --> 04:23.972
file the reports,
all while wearing a heavy cloak. Ugh.

04:24.681 --> 04:25.515
[whimpering]

04:26.140 --> 04:29.560
Please, no. I can't leave
when she's so sick, not yet.

04:29.644 --> 04:32.605
[crying] Please, not until
my granddaughter has recovered.

04:32.689 --> 04:35.275
I need more time. [sobs] Just a bit more.

04:35.358 --> 04:37.193
Unfortunately, you're mistaken.

04:37.986 --> 04:38.820
It's not you.

04:39.862 --> 04:40.697
It's her.

04:40.780 --> 04:43.658
[cries out] No, no, no! It can't--

04:43.741 --> 04:47.912
But even then, the law had questions.
Because wherever I went, death followed.

04:48.496 --> 04:50.873
Interpol may still have questions.

04:50.957 --> 04:54.002
I get it. So why did you let
Ms. Ki Ka-young hit you?

04:55.086 --> 04:57.213
Getting hit is part of the playbook too?

04:57.297 --> 04:58.423
[sighs softly]

05:00.174 --> 05:01.009
Mm.

05:01.718 --> 05:04.554
If you know all this,
Iblis knows all this too.

05:05.805 --> 05:07.307
-[scoffs]
-Of course.

05:07.390 --> 05:10.143
I keep eyes on the day,
while Sade watches the night.

05:10.935 --> 05:11.769
[huffs]

05:14.230 --> 05:16.107
[Sang-hyeok] Wait,
you're hogging them both?

05:16.190 --> 05:18.192
-I'm fighting against myself.
-Jeez.

05:18.276 --> 05:20.653
You're an adult
and you spend all your hours here?

05:20.737 --> 05:23.364
-Don't you have a job, mister?
-I work. I'm a genie, okay?

05:23.948 --> 05:26.075
And since I live for eternity,
I'm still an infant.

05:26.659 --> 05:28.661
Hmm. That means I'm older.

05:29.412 --> 05:31.372
Hey, you squirt! Get lost!

05:32.290 --> 05:34.751
No wonder Ka-young doesn't like
being around you.

05:38.504 --> 05:39.672
What did you say?

05:40.256 --> 05:41.883
Sorry for calling you squirt.

05:41.966 --> 05:44.135
Ki Ka-young. What does she tell you?

05:44.969 --> 05:47.930
I should be the one doing the disliking,
but you're saying she dislikes me?

05:48.931 --> 05:50.767
Tell me what you know, Sang-hyeok.

05:51.976 --> 05:52.935
[Sade] Master.

05:53.603 --> 05:55.438
[punching keys]

05:55.521 --> 05:57.982
Ejllael went to
the lump of clay's house? Why?

05:58.066 --> 06:00.443
Apparently, he was acting all charming,

06:00.526 --> 06:02.403
and offered to take her
to the moment she died.

06:02.487 --> 06:03.529
To the moment she died?

06:07.825 --> 06:09.160
[sighs] I feel bad.

06:09.243 --> 06:10.161
Then what?

06:10.244 --> 06:14.123
After he said that, Master's master
told Ejllael to get lost before she…

06:14.749 --> 06:15.875
-gave it to him.
-[sighs]

06:16.459 --> 06:18.544
When she's in a bad mood,
I don't get dinner.

06:19.879 --> 06:20.922
I better go check on her.

06:22.340 --> 06:23.257
Cover that man's eyes.

06:24.759 --> 06:25.676
That "man"?

06:26.552 --> 06:28.221
Ki Ka-young! [panting lightly]

06:28.930 --> 06:30.139
[gasps]

06:31.140 --> 06:33.059
Wait, that's my carpet…

06:33.810 --> 06:35.353
Oh, she's using it to--

06:35.978 --> 06:37.480
[sighs] Uh, wait.

06:38.189 --> 06:39.482
[gasps] Huh?

06:40.274 --> 06:42.276
You're wearing designer clothes.

06:43.277 --> 06:45.822
You're doing chores dressed like that?

06:46.823 --> 06:48.616
Ka-young isn't gonna be happy about that.

06:48.699 --> 06:51.702
My fashion sense will only improve
if I keep wearing things like this.

06:52.411 --> 06:54.247
All right. Hungry? I made some steaks.

06:55.164 --> 06:57.333
Ka-young won't be home till late,
so leave her some.

06:57.917 --> 06:59.627
Where is she? She wasn't at work.

07:02.588 --> 07:03.464
Oh.

07:04.507 --> 07:06.092
Today is the 4th.

07:08.302 --> 07:10.304
[somber music plays]

07:26.654 --> 07:29.907
Don't you want to know?
Would you like to learn the truth?

07:38.791 --> 07:40.960
[soft rumbling]

07:53.598 --> 07:56.559
[Iblis] You really are trying your best
to die, aren't you?

07:57.393 --> 07:58.269
That's cheating.

07:58.853 --> 08:01.564
So what was even the point
of bringing us back together again?

08:02.690 --> 08:06.486
[Iblis] Based on how you've been,
it's not because He wanted me to be happy.

08:08.029 --> 08:11.324
I don't know His intentions either.
But if you die, it'll be by my hands.

08:12.158 --> 08:14.702
You could say that's the reason
we met again.

08:15.411 --> 08:17.330
[rumbling, whooshing]

08:26.422 --> 08:28.424
[somber music continues]

08:45.107 --> 08:48.945
[woman] Your daughter, Yoo Jeong-hwa,
hasn't been to school for over a month.

08:49.028 --> 08:50.029
[sighing]

08:53.282 --> 08:54.450
[cell phone vibrates]

08:58.454 --> 08:59.330
Oh.

08:59.914 --> 09:00.748
Shit!

09:04.502 --> 09:05.920
Tell me where this is.

09:06.003 --> 09:09.799
Don't you dare say anything about privacy!
I'll call the police, got that?

09:10.383 --> 09:13.594
She's my daughter, and the boy she's with
is a minor. Understand?

09:15.221 --> 09:16.764
-[Jeong-hwa] Cover the left.
-[unlocks]

09:18.891 --> 09:22.353
-Fucking annoying. Damn it.
-We're dead again. We keep on dying.

09:22.853 --> 09:24.397
If you just played decently!

09:24.981 --> 09:28.651
-[boy] You're one to talk. You suck too.
-[Jeong-hwa speaks indistinctly]

09:30.861 --> 09:35.032
How long do other people
generally wait before making it?

09:36.367 --> 09:37.827
Their third and final wish?

09:41.080 --> 09:44.208
One guy held onto that third wish
for 72 years.

09:44.292 --> 09:45.960
[chuckles dryly] Oh, wow.

09:47.795 --> 09:48.879
I get that, though.

09:50.298 --> 09:54.135
I'm caught between a feeling of defeat,
because it's my last,

09:54.719 --> 09:57.138
and a great hope
that it could repair everything.

09:57.888 --> 09:59.390
So I don't want to let it go.

10:00.558 --> 10:01.892
[breathes heavily]

10:03.019 --> 10:05.605
So, then, what did that person wish for?

10:06.230 --> 10:08.608
Humans tend to make
their first wish immediately

10:09.191 --> 10:11.736
because they worry
that their luck will vanish.

10:12.570 --> 10:16.782
They use their second wish to make up for
the first wish that they made in a hurry.

10:17.908 --> 10:20.870
They blame themselves for not having
wished for something greater.

10:21.537 --> 10:24.915
Then they torture themselves,
clutching onto their last wish.

10:24.999 --> 10:28.294
They look and look and look
for that perfect wish.

10:29.879 --> 10:32.548
So, after 72 years,
he made his final wish.

10:33.215 --> 10:35.301
And he wished for me to forget that…

10:36.218 --> 10:38.929
he'd already used two. [chuckles]

10:39.013 --> 10:40.514
[soft suspenseful music plays]

10:40.598 --> 10:42.725
He figured out the greatest thing of all.

10:46.228 --> 10:47.146
Does that…

10:48.105 --> 10:48.939
work?

10:52.026 --> 10:53.110
Why don't you try it?

10:54.987 --> 10:56.614
Wish for that if you're curious.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.116
[chuckles smugly]

10:59.200 --> 11:01.202
[music intensifies]

11:04.789 --> 11:05.623
[music stops]

11:11.128 --> 11:13.130
[chuckles softly] Hmm.

11:15.966 --> 11:16.842
[gasps]

11:17.426 --> 11:19.095
[gasps] Oh, my goodness.

11:22.139 --> 11:24.392
[Ka-young] Always store the purses
in their pouches.

11:24.475 --> 11:26.018
Don't use them on rainy days.

11:26.102 --> 11:28.396
Hot pink Crocs pair well with nothing.

11:28.479 --> 11:31.107
Sneakers or heels with this outfit.

11:31.190 --> 11:33.984
Pair these shoes with this bag
for something chic.

11:34.068 --> 11:35.653
No fruit knives in the purses.

11:35.736 --> 11:37.196
This girl is something.

11:38.239 --> 11:40.241
I get it. This is how you do it.

11:40.825 --> 11:42.326
What have we got here?

11:43.369 --> 11:45.037
[inhales deeply] Hmm.

11:45.955 --> 11:46.831
[takes off paper]

11:47.790 --> 11:50.000
Today is your day.

11:51.293 --> 11:53.087
[light peppy music plays]

11:53.170 --> 11:54.046
[gasps]

11:58.300 --> 11:59.593
[gasping excitedly]

12:08.894 --> 12:09.728
Oh?

12:11.772 --> 12:12.606
[chuckles]

12:13.274 --> 12:16.026
How much? Just for one?

12:16.652 --> 12:19.238
That's outrageous!
You get a loaf of bread for that.

12:20.573 --> 12:24.118
You're wearing designer heels
and a blouse from the latest collection.

12:24.702 --> 12:26.370
And macarons are too expensive?

12:28.706 --> 12:30.166
You're a strange one.

12:30.916 --> 12:33.919
[chuckles] Of course I am. Who isn't?

12:35.045 --> 12:39.592
Next time, come to my place. I'll make you
a hotteok as big as your head. [chuckles]

12:41.218 --> 12:43.929
It's on the house.
The owner here is a patient of mine

12:44.013 --> 12:46.599
and they still need a few more implants.

12:48.350 --> 12:51.729
Then we should pay for these. It's not
like their implants are free, right?

12:51.812 --> 12:52.688
[chuckles softly]

12:52.771 --> 12:54.773
Okay, what have we got here?

12:58.319 --> 13:00.821
-[squeals] Too sweet.
-[chuckles]

13:00.905 --> 13:02.239
Two would be too many.

13:02.907 --> 13:04.825
An old-fashioned palate.

13:04.909 --> 13:07.703
And an up-front and personal invite
to your home.

13:07.786 --> 13:10.331
[inhales sharply]
What on earth could be your deal?

13:15.669 --> 13:16.629
My deal?

13:17.379 --> 13:19.965
Life has been a tiny bit difficult,

13:20.049 --> 13:23.344
and now it's a tiny bit more fun. Mm?

13:23.928 --> 13:25.596
[both laugh]

13:27.515 --> 13:29.850
[Mi-ju] Have some, have some.
[chuckles]

13:29.934 --> 13:30.768
Mm.

13:31.977 --> 13:33.938
[Heung-rye] It just doesn't
make any sense to me.

13:34.522 --> 13:38.067
Pan-geum, she-- Just because
she's all the way out in Hawaii,

13:38.150 --> 13:40.986
it doesn't make any sense
that we haven't heard from her.

13:41.070 --> 13:43.656
Some crazy crap is going on.

13:43.739 --> 13:44.823
Mm, that's true.

13:45.741 --> 13:49.119
It's one thing not to call us,
but she could still answer her phone.

13:49.703 --> 13:52.706
Plus, that complete stranger moving
into her house the moment she leaves

13:52.790 --> 13:54.416
makes you think something's off.

13:55.251 --> 13:59.296
I know. I saw that young woman
and Dr. Choi eating macarons.

13:59.880 --> 14:02.258
I also did see Ka-young and that girl.

14:02.341 --> 14:05.219
They were digging up
Pan-geum's pepper field at nighttime.

14:05.970 --> 14:07.304
Is that all connected?

14:07.388 --> 14:09.682
The chili field? Oh, my, my goodness!

14:09.765 --> 14:11.809
Ka-young did it! She finally snapped!

14:11.892 --> 14:15.563
It all makes sense. She's a psychopath,
so she killed her grandma and buried her!

14:16.355 --> 14:17.731
-That's too much. No.
-Come on.

14:17.815 --> 14:20.276
She wouldn't? How can you be sure? Right?

14:20.359 --> 14:22.069
That bitch has gotta be involved.

14:22.152 --> 14:23.988
So please call Chang-sik, now!

14:25.447 --> 14:26.282
[sighs]

14:27.032 --> 14:30.119
She's staying here as a guest.
She wanted to experience the country.

14:30.202 --> 14:33.330
Cut the crap.
If she's really here for half a year,

14:33.414 --> 14:35.583
then why did she come out
of Pan-geum's room?

14:35.666 --> 14:37.710
Okay, now everyone remain calm. Calm down.

14:37.793 --> 14:40.170
These elders have
reasonable concerns and suspicions.

14:40.254 --> 14:43.007
I propose you answer all questions
with the utmost sincerity.

14:43.924 --> 14:46.427
Now tell us, where is your grandmother?

14:47.553 --> 14:50.681
Hawaii.
She's always dreamed of going there.

14:50.764 --> 14:53.851
She wanted to go when she was younger,
but never did and regretted it.

14:54.560 --> 14:57.771
Hawaii? As in "Hawaii" Hawaii?

14:58.606 --> 15:01.567
-She went all alone?
-Will you stop going on about the past?

15:02.234 --> 15:04.028
-Huh?
-She flew to Hawaii!

15:04.111 --> 15:05.654
-Yes?
-She's not answering her phone!

15:05.738 --> 15:07.031
-No one can reach her!
-Oh.

15:07.114 --> 15:08.699
All you need to know
is that she's gone.

15:08.782 --> 15:11.535
There. There. What did I tell you?
She said she's gone.

15:11.619 --> 15:13.203
What did I tell you? She killed her!

15:13.287 --> 15:15.539
-[women gasp]
-This one must be an accomplice.

15:15.623 --> 15:18.292
Seongnim! Why would you
suggest something so--

15:18.375 --> 15:19.293
"Seongnim"?

15:23.797 --> 15:24.757
Oh…

15:25.966 --> 15:29.637
Isn't that what you call each other
out here in the countryside?

15:30.179 --> 15:32.222
That's what I've seen on TV.
[chuckles nervously]

15:32.306 --> 15:35.643
Oh, oh, look at that weasel
squinting her eyes with that phony smile.

15:35.726 --> 15:38.062
Look at that!
You're not fooling anyone, wench!

15:38.562 --> 15:42.149
You, call your grandma right now!
I want to see her with my own eyes!

15:42.775 --> 15:45.152
She's right.
None of us can get ahold of her.

15:45.235 --> 15:46.570
Aren't you worried at all?

15:47.696 --> 15:50.240
What did I tell you?
Of course she can't call her.

15:50.324 --> 15:51.951
You, spit it out!

15:52.034 --> 15:54.119
Your grandma,
you murdered her, didn't you?

15:54.203 --> 15:55.245
Hey, what did you--

15:55.871 --> 15:57.581
You can't. Mm.

15:58.832 --> 16:00.334
[line connects, rings]

16:00.417 --> 16:01.251
[Chang-sik] Hey.

16:02.127 --> 16:03.712
Oh, I think it's going through!

16:04.630 --> 16:06.840
We've called, but she never
answers or returns our call.

16:06.924 --> 16:07.967
MS. OH PAN-GEUM
CONNECTING

16:08.592 --> 16:10.302
[line continues ringing]

16:10.386 --> 16:11.679
-[call connects]
-Huh?

16:12.388 --> 16:15.057
Oh, hey. What? Did something happen?

16:16.100 --> 16:17.476
I'm having a great time in Hawaii.

16:17.559 --> 16:20.646
[Chang-sik] Good, great!
You're doing fine. It's Chang-sik!

16:20.729 --> 16:23.232
-Everyone, say hello.
-[Bok-ja laughing]

16:23.315 --> 16:26.694
[Chang-sik] Is it nighttime there?
Whoa, isn't that neat!

16:27.486 --> 16:30.572
[Pan-geum] Look over, there's the ocean.
Can you see it? Amazing, isn't it?

16:30.656 --> 16:33.117
-Hand the phone over! Give it!
-Okay. It's a video call--

16:33.200 --> 16:35.452
-You're really something, you know that?
-[Bok-ja] Hello.

16:35.536 --> 16:38.497
You went all the way there by yourself?
I heard you had a extra ticket.

16:38.580 --> 16:40.541
[Chang-sik] All right,
let's all take turns.

16:40.624 --> 16:43.669
Oh, my, look at all those flowers.
[laughs]

16:44.253 --> 16:47.214
Heavens, you look wonderful. [laughing]

16:47.297 --> 16:50.801
Hey, why didn't you answer your phone?
When are you coming back?

16:50.884 --> 16:54.471
Uh, I'm thinking of staying
for a few more months.

16:54.555 --> 16:57.599
Ka-young is grown up
and can take care of herself.

16:57.683 --> 17:00.102
My eldest daughter asked me
to live with her.

17:00.769 --> 17:02.604
-Oh, anyone there? Hello?
-[Ok-nam] Uh, what?

17:02.688 --> 17:04.815
Huh? Something's wrong
with the connection.

17:04.898 --> 17:06.567
My phone doesn't get good reception here.

17:06.650 --> 17:08.861
-Can you bring back some jojoba oil?
-You're all frozen.

17:08.944 --> 17:09.903
Oh, the call dropped.

17:11.488 --> 17:15.451
Anyway, you all saw that she's alive.
And you suspected Ms. Ki for nothing!

17:15.534 --> 17:17.703
Enough, enough.
Clear out, everyone. Clear out.

17:17.786 --> 17:21.040
-All right, we have strawberries to pick.
-[Heung-rye grumbles]

17:21.123 --> 17:22.291
Let's go!

17:22.374 --> 17:26.253
You could've just called her when
we asked. Instead of acting suspiciously,

17:26.336 --> 17:28.255
you know, as if you were
hiding something fishy.

17:28.338 --> 17:30.883
Who wouldn't suspect you?
Act normal for once.

17:34.219 --> 17:36.221
[somber music plays]

17:39.767 --> 17:40.934
[Ka-young sighs]

17:42.561 --> 17:43.395
Uh…

17:44.104 --> 17:46.607
Sorry, I was planning
to drop by city hall.

17:47.524 --> 17:48.942
From now on, I'll stay here.

17:49.777 --> 17:53.280
I'm sorry. I cause you
such a headache. Gosh.

17:55.574 --> 17:56.408
[sighs]

18:01.038 --> 18:01.872
[sighs]

18:06.251 --> 18:11.131
You believed you were gonna be great
at creating wishes without any flaws? Ha!

18:11.882 --> 18:12.925
What, no thank you?

18:13.926 --> 18:15.385
So this is what it's like

18:16.303 --> 18:17.554
to get what I deserve…

18:19.515 --> 18:21.475
in exchange for wishes from Satan.

18:32.861 --> 18:34.321
[sighs]

18:44.832 --> 18:45.916
Hello there.

18:47.876 --> 18:49.795
I'm a student researching facial features.

18:49.878 --> 18:52.256
[gasps] Your soul is very pure indeed.

18:52.840 --> 18:53.674
[scoffs]

18:55.759 --> 18:58.512
Of course it is. I am of the genie.

18:58.595 --> 19:00.013
But something's wrong, isn't it?

19:01.431 --> 19:02.474
How do you know?

19:04.184 --> 19:07.104
I should be happy to see
my enemy in pain, but I'm not.

19:07.813 --> 19:11.400
-What's going on?
-Yes. I see unhappiness inside of you.

19:11.483 --> 19:14.153
An ancestor of yours died
far from home on the street.

19:15.070 --> 19:18.031
My ancestors are immortal.
It's my brothers who died.

19:19.992 --> 19:21.952
Most were killed
in the war against the angels.

19:24.079 --> 19:25.873
I'm just helping you
get your facts straight.

19:26.498 --> 19:27.374
[pats]

19:27.875 --> 19:30.127
Ah. I understand.

19:30.961 --> 19:32.462
Then, best wishes to you.

19:34.006 --> 19:36.633
Where are you going?
I barely made it past the introduction.

19:37.467 --> 19:39.219
That war went on for 300 years.

19:39.303 --> 19:41.763
[music playing faintly over speakers]

19:47.352 --> 19:48.562
Heading home for the night?

19:50.731 --> 19:51.565
Hey, Ms. Lee.

19:52.941 --> 19:55.694
[gasps] I'm sorry,
would you mind repeating that?

19:56.278 --> 20:00.991
I can't hear things at all. I need to look
at your face to comfortably read lips.

20:01.575 --> 20:04.244
-[woman] Your latte, miss. It's ready.
-I didn't know. I'm sorry.

20:04.328 --> 20:05.704
[louder] Your latte is ready.

20:10.709 --> 20:13.795
I was born this way.
I've been practicing since I was young.

20:14.755 --> 20:17.007
But I remain deaf to heaven's secrets.

20:17.090 --> 20:18.008
Good night.

20:21.136 --> 20:22.179
What was that?

20:23.055 --> 20:26.683
Was she just going off about the reckoning
or something like that?

20:27.768 --> 20:30.812
[Irem] I was born
from a single wisp of white smoke,

20:30.896 --> 20:34.107
exhaled from the hookah pipe
of the angel, Ejllael.

20:35.734 --> 20:39.238
When my master created me,
he blocked my ears so I would never hear

20:39.321 --> 20:40.948
-any secrets from heaven.
-[girl screams]

20:41.031 --> 20:43.492
You're the only one
who's been nice to me all day!

20:43.575 --> 20:44.952
-[horn honking]
-[tires screeching]

20:45.035 --> 20:47.955
-[crashing]
-[Iblis groans] Bad luck.

20:49.331 --> 20:52.542
-[chiming and whooshing]
-[indistinct chatter]

20:55.963 --> 20:57.005
[Iblis] Huh?

20:57.756 --> 20:59.174
[chatter and laughter]

20:59.967 --> 21:00.801
Hmm?

21:03.553 --> 21:04.388
Hmm?

21:06.890 --> 21:09.017
[clamoring]

21:10.852 --> 21:12.646
[cheering]

21:17.734 --> 21:19.069
This your first time here, Unc?

21:20.570 --> 21:23.573
Hey, Auntie. That's not the restroom.
Go outside. Go.

21:24.366 --> 21:25.659
You must all be related.

21:25.742 --> 21:28.120
What's going on? You want to play or not?

21:28.704 --> 21:30.706
I don't even know what's going on.

21:30.789 --> 21:34.584
And, most importantly,
I have no money. [giggling]

21:34.668 --> 21:36.086
Don't worry about things like that.

21:36.169 --> 21:38.630
Learn the game as you play,
that's what you do.

21:38.714 --> 21:40.299
And I can just lend you the money.

21:40.799 --> 21:43.427
How about one million to start?
10% paid in advance.

21:44.511 --> 21:47.556
Wait, you're just giving me this?

21:48.348 --> 21:49.766
[gasps] Thank you.

21:51.643 --> 21:52.853
Are you the boss
in this group?

21:54.980 --> 21:57.024
Don't worry. I'll do this very slowly.

21:57.107 --> 22:00.110
-[sirens approaching]
-[amusing music plays]

22:05.407 --> 22:07.617
We've decided to drop
the sexual assault charges.

22:07.701 --> 22:10.162
Turns out, people over there
rub noses as a greeting.

22:10.245 --> 22:12.122
-[both laugh]
-Okay.

22:12.205 --> 22:14.333
Once your guardian arrives, you may leave.

22:14.416 --> 22:16.084
M-- My guardian?

22:16.793 --> 22:20.589
Hey, is it-- Can I just go?
Didn't you see my beating the other day?

22:26.178 --> 22:27.179
[Ka-young sighs]

22:28.430 --> 22:31.558
Sexual assault?
First, you dine and dash, and now this?

22:32.267 --> 22:33.643
[cracking knuckles]

22:33.727 --> 22:35.687
-Put the clip in your hair.
-[sighs]

22:35.771 --> 22:36.730
Put it there now!

22:38.273 --> 22:41.318
-At least let me explain.
-[cracking knuckles]

22:42.110 --> 22:44.029
Seriously, this is just unfair.

22:45.864 --> 22:47.991
[Ka-young grunts] Come over here.

22:48.575 --> 22:52.120
[grunting] You say unfair? This unfair?

22:52.996 --> 22:54.790
-[Iblis grunts]
-Get over here!

22:55.290 --> 22:57.167
[grunting]

23:01.088 --> 23:03.507
Come here! [grunting]

23:09.304 --> 23:10.388
Two left.

23:11.681 --> 23:13.016
Two of them left now.

23:13.558 --> 23:15.018
Two left.

23:15.811 --> 23:16.728
Two left.

23:17.312 --> 23:18.438
Two left.

23:19.272 --> 23:20.273
Two left.

23:21.316 --> 23:22.567
SA FAMILY GAMJA-TANG

23:22.651 --> 23:25.987
[people cheering, chattering]

23:26.655 --> 23:28.073
Sh… Shit.

23:28.156 --> 23:30.659
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
10,000,000 WON

23:30.742 --> 23:32.744
[breathing heavily]

23:32.828 --> 23:34.287
How is this real?

23:37.124 --> 23:38.708
CHEONGPUNGHO BANK

23:38.792 --> 23:41.878
That bitch has so much money, but
her daily transfer limit is just 10,000!

23:42.379 --> 23:45.006
[breathes heavily] This just won't work.

23:45.090 --> 23:47.843
Once her money's transferred,
it's an immediate investigation.

23:48.510 --> 23:50.137
I'll figure out the rest myself.

23:50.220 --> 23:51.721
But here's my second wish.

23:51.805 --> 23:54.266
Increase Ki Ka-young's transfer limits
to the max.

23:54.349 --> 23:55.684
[rumbling]

24:02.357 --> 24:03.191
[knock on door]

24:08.905 --> 24:10.949
Why did you lock the break room?

24:11.032 --> 24:13.368
Well, hurry and get out.
Ki Ka-young would like to see you.

24:24.838 --> 24:27.174
Increase my daily transfer limit
to the max.

24:29.259 --> 24:30.302
[sighs in delight]

24:31.219 --> 24:32.053
Sure.

24:33.597 --> 24:34.556
The limit's 50,000.

24:38.560 --> 24:40.103
Fill these out here and here.

24:41.396 --> 24:42.355
And down here too.

24:42.439 --> 24:44.441
[suspenseful music playing]

24:45.442 --> 24:46.776
[laughs maniacally]

24:53.617 --> 24:55.619
[printer whirring]

24:59.623 --> 25:02.167
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
50,000,000 WON

25:02.250 --> 25:03.960
[gasps, screams]

25:04.044 --> 25:05.295
[music intensifies]

25:11.051 --> 25:15.013
GU BO-GYEONG, JULY 12, 2024
MADE HER SECOND WISH

25:15.096 --> 25:18.600
INCREASE KI KA-YOUNG'S TRANSFER LIMIT

25:22.020 --> 25:24.814
All of the humans I've seen
love getting money, but hate losing it.

25:24.898 --> 25:26.900
Where do you stand?
Don't you hate losing it?

25:28.443 --> 25:30.445
I'm using it quickly to avoid losing it.

25:31.529 --> 25:33.073
It's meaningful to lose money

25:33.156 --> 25:35.659
if it's in exchange
for another type of validation.

25:36.243 --> 25:37.786
It just validates that I was arrogant.

25:38.370 --> 25:39.246
[chuckles softly]

25:40.830 --> 25:43.416
So you can stop giggling.
I know I'm losing.

25:48.296 --> 25:49.965
-Why were you there in the water?
-Hmm?

25:50.674 --> 25:52.342
You were making the bubbles, weren't you?

25:53.260 --> 25:54.928
I can go wherever I wanna go.

25:56.680 --> 25:58.807
It's not like you own the ocean.

26:02.519 --> 26:04.813
Do you happen to hate something?
Anything in particular?

26:05.480 --> 26:06.564
I'm thinking garlic?

26:07.190 --> 26:08.525
-[gasps]
-Or a wooden stake?

26:08.608 --> 26:09.651
Perhaps a cross?

26:09.734 --> 26:11.486
[laughing]

26:14.322 --> 26:16.574
I particularly hate you.

26:17.242 --> 26:18.285
Get out!

26:18.368 --> 26:20.620
[upbeat music playing over speakers]

26:29.629 --> 26:32.090
Oh, you're here. You found your way.

26:32.173 --> 26:36.386
I'm here, yes. Although a newbie like me
can't really do anything.

26:36.469 --> 26:38.763
I was a complete mess
when I first started too.

26:39.264 --> 26:42.892
-But you've tried other sports, right?
-In the past, I did some yoga.

26:42.976 --> 26:45.687
I could put my foot behind my neck,
you know? That kind of thing.

26:45.770 --> 26:47.897
-[chuckles]
-But I can't do that anymore.

26:48.648 --> 26:50.108
I made my way here to learn.

26:50.734 --> 26:53.445
I wanna know how to defend myself
and how to protect someone too.

26:54.112 --> 26:56.156
Okay. Hit this.
Punch it as hard as you can.

26:56.239 --> 26:57.532
-[grunts]
-Whoa!

26:57.615 --> 27:00.493
-Whoa! That's shocking. My goodness.
-Whoa, what was that?

27:00.577 --> 27:03.038
-[gasps]
-Whoa. You could get us into trouble.

27:03.705 --> 27:04.748
You make a lot of money?

27:05.749 --> 27:07.500
You might have to get them a new one.

27:07.584 --> 27:10.045
Oh, really? Can we fix it?

27:10.545 --> 27:11.755
I'm just teasing.

27:13.673 --> 27:16.092
-You were joking?
-[laughing]

27:16.176 --> 27:17.844
Come fight me, then. Come on.

27:20.055 --> 27:20.972
Whoa!

27:22.557 --> 27:23.933
Did you see the mansion?

27:24.017 --> 27:27.312
[blows] You think the all folks
in the front yard are related? [slurps]

27:27.395 --> 27:29.773
They looked like guards to me.
Not relatives at all.

27:30.899 --> 27:32.650
Nope. Can't fool me.

27:33.860 --> 27:35.570
They're not related nor guards either.

27:37.030 --> 27:39.574
There's something happening
in our little village.

27:40.533 --> 27:41.409
They are…

27:43.536 --> 27:44.371
soldiers.

27:44.454 --> 27:45.622
-Soldiers, really?
-An army?

27:45.705 --> 27:47.248
Yes. Military.

27:47.749 --> 27:50.377
GOBLIN STATIONERY

27:51.169 --> 27:52.754
[joystick clicking]

28:01.638 --> 28:03.807
Mister, how did you get that money?

28:04.474 --> 28:06.810
-You were always broke until now.
-[chuckles]

28:06.893 --> 28:08.812
-[Ka-young] That's it, stop.
-But why?

28:10.021 --> 28:11.147
Empty your pockets.

28:11.856 --> 28:12.690
Really?

28:22.534 --> 28:23.952
[laughing]

28:25.412 --> 28:26.579
Dark methods were involved.

28:28.123 --> 28:29.958
[music playing over game]

28:30.041 --> 28:31.584
Game's on me.

28:32.710 --> 28:35.547
-For real? You're serious?
-[chuckles]

28:42.554 --> 28:43.638
What happened to your arms?

28:44.514 --> 28:46.307
Dark family matters were involved.

28:48.518 --> 28:50.645
Hey, um, want me to tell you a secret?

28:52.397 --> 28:54.190
This is a very important secret.

28:54.274 --> 28:57.986
-[woman] Run quickly! Run away quickly!
-[man] You piece of shit, get back here!

28:58.069 --> 29:00.321
[woman] Why take it out on the kid
when it's your fault?

29:00.405 --> 29:02.949
[man] I told you to get
an overdraft account, you bitch!

29:03.032 --> 29:05.702
[woman] You took all my money, asshole!

29:06.286 --> 29:08.663
[Sang-hyeok] That was when I saw an angel.

29:10.707 --> 29:13.293
You did? I see them once in a while.

29:13.376 --> 29:14.294
Are you ready?

29:14.377 --> 29:16.129
I'm telling you what I saw.

29:16.713 --> 29:20.175
So I prayed to the angel. I begged him
to make Mom's friend go away.

29:20.800 --> 29:22.677
That stupid jerk you saw
doesn't grant wishes.

29:22.761 --> 29:25.972
-He's basically in it for himself.
-You don't have to believe me.

29:26.055 --> 29:30.101
As soon as I'm a little bit bigger,
I'm planning to beat up that man.

29:31.019 --> 29:33.188
But it takes a long time to grow up.

29:40.069 --> 29:43.114
-All right, give me a quarter.
-You have so much right now.

29:43.698 --> 29:46.993
I can grant you the wish you want.
However, it's not free.

29:47.786 --> 29:49.662
You won't know this,
but the wish specialist--

29:49.746 --> 29:52.624
Oh, I just won! [laughing]

29:53.792 --> 29:57.504
I'm willing to believe you once,
because I deliberately just lost to you.

29:58.254 --> 30:00.089
Hey. Wow.

30:00.173 --> 30:02.425
[laughs] You're worse than Satan.

30:03.009 --> 30:05.136
All right. Only until you become an adult.

30:05.720 --> 30:08.932
You're 12 years old now, so let's see…

30:09.015 --> 30:11.935
They'll maul him so he can't
get out of bed for about seven years.

30:12.018 --> 30:13.978
[screaming]

30:15.480 --> 30:16.481
[thuds]

30:16.564 --> 30:18.942
-[screams in pain]
-[tense music plays]

30:22.362 --> 30:24.823
My back. My legs. [groans]

30:27.200 --> 30:28.576
[Iblis] I've seen you before.

30:28.660 --> 30:29.994
[grunts, gasps]

30:31.329 --> 30:34.999
Who are you?
Help, please! Send help, please!

30:36.334 --> 30:37.168
Help?

30:37.752 --> 30:40.129
-[grunts]
-There's no help here.

30:41.130 --> 30:43.007
No real man would beat a little boy.

30:43.091 --> 30:45.218
You make Satan look like a saint.

30:46.261 --> 30:47.303
Hang in there.

30:49.681 --> 30:54.185
Long ago, I fought for 300 years
to protect my brothers.

30:55.019 --> 30:56.604
At this moment in time, I've chosen…

30:58.523 --> 31:00.984
to start another war
for a brother who needs me.

31:01.693 --> 31:03.027
[whimpering]

31:04.821 --> 31:06.573
Sang-hyeok's my rival and friend.

31:07.532 --> 31:09.200
And he chose to be my older brother.

31:11.202 --> 31:13.288
That's why you're suffering right now.

31:13.371 --> 31:14.372
[whistles]

31:15.164 --> 31:18.251
[whimpering]

31:19.210 --> 31:22.046
-[yelping] No, please! Help me!
-[dogs snarling]

31:22.130 --> 31:25.717
I was wrong! I shouldn't have!
I won't do it again! Please! Help me!

31:25.800 --> 31:28.636
-Aw.
-[shrieking] Please stop!

31:28.720 --> 31:30.680
I'm not really much for helping people.

31:30.763 --> 31:33.433
-[dogs growling and biting]
-[man screaming]

31:47.780 --> 31:49.782
[pensive music plays]

32:00.209 --> 32:02.003
[whooshing]

32:06.591 --> 32:09.052
Why are you following me around?
You not busy enough?

32:10.219 --> 32:12.347
You brought a man to the desert
to have him mauled,

32:12.430 --> 32:14.599
and I had to get an ambulance
and clean up the mess!

32:14.682 --> 32:16.601
Why do you keep
plunging the world into chaos?

32:17.185 --> 32:19.562
Who are you fooling
pretending to be a good guy?

32:20.229 --> 32:22.190
I've actually been thinking about that.

32:22.273 --> 32:25.485
Have you ever thought I might've been
the good guy, and the bad guy was you?

32:26.069 --> 32:30.490
[sighs] I promise to use a very
blunt scythe when I slit your throat.

32:30.990 --> 32:33.493
-I'll have to hack for hours.
-That's right.

32:33.576 --> 32:35.495
We're not so different, you and I.

32:36.663 --> 32:39.499
How do you have time to talk?
Don't you need to see Ki Ka-young again?

32:41.209 --> 32:43.044
Ah. Don't tell me you're afraid of her.

32:43.628 --> 32:46.130
[exhales sharply] What?

32:47.674 --> 32:49.008
You concerned I'll see her again?

32:51.219 --> 32:53.346
What do you even want to show Ki Ka-young?

32:53.888 --> 32:56.975
Well? How cruel I am?
Or the wishes she made?

32:57.058 --> 32:59.727
I took my punishment for 983 years.

33:01.354 --> 33:02.480
That not enough?

33:04.273 --> 33:06.526
[laughs]

33:07.902 --> 33:09.237
How funny it is.

33:10.530 --> 33:14.450
A mere thousand years
is nothing relative to eternity.

33:16.327 --> 33:17.495
A drop in the bucket.

33:23.459 --> 33:26.671
I looked at all the parts, and I couldn't
find what's wrong with the watch.

33:26.754 --> 33:27.588
That so?

33:30.675 --> 33:34.846
The watch hands were spinning backwards.
And incredibly fast.

33:34.929 --> 33:39.600
I've never had this kind of issue before,
and I've worked here for over ten years.

33:39.684 --> 33:42.937
For what it's worth, it's impossible
for watch hands to do that.

33:44.439 --> 33:46.524
[ticking]

33:47.567 --> 33:48.901
[ticking grows louder]

33:50.737 --> 33:53.156
-Huh?
-[rapid ticking]

33:55.408 --> 33:56.993
Can I really not get myself inside?

34:05.209 --> 34:06.461
What does the inscription say?

34:06.544 --> 34:10.089
It says you shouldn't shake it,
or an ill-tempered genie might get angry.

34:15.219 --> 34:16.054
[camera clicks]

34:18.431 --> 34:19.474
TRANSLATE

34:21.392 --> 34:24.187
SHELF LIFE IS INFINITE
FROM DATE OF REMAKING: OCTOBER 24, 1061

34:25.772 --> 34:26.689
So he lied.

34:27.565 --> 34:31.903
If that's when the lamp was made,
and he claims he was there for 983 years,

34:32.779 --> 34:33.946
there's a gap of 20 years.

34:37.200 --> 34:38.367
Is he getting scammed?

34:40.036 --> 34:41.120
What is this?

34:47.043 --> 34:49.212
[snuffling]

34:52.131 --> 34:54.675
-[sniffing]
-[suspenseful music plays]

35:02.558 --> 35:03.851
[sniffing]

35:09.065 --> 35:09.982
Who are they?

35:11.275 --> 35:13.152
Why do they sit like that for hours?

35:14.070 --> 35:15.530
We might need to report it.

35:21.661 --> 35:22.703
They keep staring all day.

35:23.287 --> 35:25.164
What's up with that?
What are they looking at?

35:27.583 --> 35:30.419
[chauffeur] As a former member
of the Reconnaissance Unit,

35:30.503 --> 35:32.046
I know when there are eyes on us.

35:33.756 --> 35:35.007
Two in the bushes.

35:36.551 --> 35:37.802
Two more in the mansion.

35:38.803 --> 35:40.054
Perhaps others.

35:40.930 --> 35:41.764
[sighs]

35:42.473 --> 35:45.935
Boss, what kind of life have you led
up until now?

35:49.188 --> 35:50.189
Don't you worry.

35:51.858 --> 35:53.151
You can count on me.

36:01.200 --> 36:02.451
Sir, sorry to bother you.

36:03.286 --> 36:05.371
What are you waiting for?
We've been here a while.

36:07.123 --> 36:07.957
Yeah.

36:08.791 --> 36:09.750
For my father.

36:10.459 --> 36:12.587
I've lost him.
This is where I became lost.

36:14.505 --> 36:16.215
I remember the smell of his car.

36:17.425 --> 36:18.718
[sniffing]

36:19.802 --> 36:21.971
And also my little brother, Kim Ha-neul.

36:23.181 --> 36:24.390
He's worried, you know.

36:27.435 --> 36:28.686
Your family?

36:28.769 --> 36:31.272
Could this be some sort
of short-term memory loss?

36:32.565 --> 36:34.942
Or are you wrapped up in conspiracies?

36:36.527 --> 36:39.113
-[woman 1] It's just wrong.
-[woman 2] Completely insane.

36:39.197 --> 36:42.074
He said I can't leave today
until she gets here. Can you believe that?

36:42.158 --> 36:44.660
-[woman 1] Mm.
-The freaking manager is mad to--

36:44.744 --> 36:45.578
[woman 1] So crazy.

36:45.661 --> 36:47.079
Oh, she's here. She just came in.

36:47.788 --> 36:48.623
What's going on?

36:49.707 --> 36:52.210
[scoffs] I can't believe this.

36:53.127 --> 36:54.003
Come on.

36:58.132 --> 37:00.134
[manager] Do you have anything
to say for yourself?

37:00.218 --> 37:03.012
Why is Ms. Ki Ka-young's money
being transferred

37:03.095 --> 37:05.514
every single day
into your personal account?

37:06.265 --> 37:07.099
Are you stealing?

37:07.808 --> 37:11.145
What makes you even think that? This is
the first time I'm hearing any of this.

37:11.229 --> 37:12.521
[manager laughs]

37:12.605 --> 37:15.107
You've been putting the money
from her bank account

37:15.191 --> 37:17.944
into your bank account
every day for two weeks!

37:18.027 --> 37:20.196
[scoffs] This is driving me crazy.

37:20.279 --> 37:23.532
You're saying you expect me
to spend all day checking my accounts?

37:23.616 --> 37:25.993
A large amount's being transferred
to you every day.

37:26.077 --> 37:27.495
And you claim you didn't know?

37:27.578 --> 37:30.498
And we know you've also logged repeatedly
into her account.

37:31.082 --> 37:32.291
How do you explain that?

37:32.917 --> 37:35.878
You told me to make her set up
a retirement account with us.

37:35.962 --> 37:37.964
That's why I looked,
to see how to convince her.

37:38.047 --> 37:40.091
You saw the logs, so you know already.

37:40.174 --> 37:42.927
She's the one who came in
to up her transfer limit.

37:43.010 --> 37:45.554
Why are we doing this?
If you have questions,

37:45.638 --> 37:47.598
shouldn't you be asking Ki Ka-young
about it?

37:47.682 --> 37:48.891
Wo-- Wow.

37:48.975 --> 37:53.771
Well, sir. Due to the circumstances,
we're already being investigated, so--

37:53.854 --> 37:56.357
You shut your damn trap!
I'm aware of that!

37:57.024 --> 37:58.776
[sighs] Ms. Gu, this is serious.

37:58.859 --> 38:02.238
You need to go and meet Ms. Ki Ka-young
before it spirals out.

38:02.321 --> 38:03.948
Find out what happened with her money!

38:04.031 --> 38:05.908
You're friends, right? Friends?

38:05.992 --> 38:08.953
We're all gonna get axed right away
if this isn't resolved!

38:10.538 --> 38:11.372
All right.

38:13.708 --> 38:15.793
[dark eerie music plays]

38:21.716 --> 38:24.802
Hello. See, I'm back, so now you can eat.

38:31.851 --> 38:33.102
I enjoyed reading this.

38:42.445 --> 38:45.406
HISTORY OF GORYEO

38:55.541 --> 38:56.375
Well, then,

38:57.918 --> 38:59.337
have you made your decision?

39:05.426 --> 39:07.053
[Iblis] The angels came down from heaven

39:07.136 --> 39:09.305
and began slaughtering
the genies on earth,

39:09.388 --> 39:12.266
and Ejllael was the angel
who led the charge.

39:12.350 --> 39:13.601
[chuckles]

39:13.684 --> 39:17.021
The war lasted 300 years,
and in the end, I lost.

39:17.563 --> 39:19.523
Most of my brothers died.

39:24.695 --> 39:25.821
Take me back

39:26.447 --> 39:27.531
to when I died.

39:32.078 --> 39:34.372
[low growling]

39:37.166 --> 39:38.459
[Irem hoots]

39:38.542 --> 39:42.296
[Ejllael] He is furious
that disasters and droughts

39:42.838 --> 39:44.215
have ravaged Africa.

39:45.299 --> 39:46.801
A lot of people have died.

39:47.468 --> 39:52.598
Don't meddle with them anymore
Temper yourself. Don't overdo it.

39:53.808 --> 39:56.727
By the way,
what's this face you're wearing?

39:57.728 --> 40:01.816
I've chosen a face that will be desirable
for the next thousand years.

40:03.150 --> 40:04.985
It's a face made for wish-granting.

40:06.070 --> 40:08.364
My next master will be here soon.
I'm ready.

40:08.948 --> 40:09.865
[chuckles lightly]

40:09.949 --> 40:12.159
[somber traditional music plays]

40:39.311 --> 40:41.397
[snarling]

40:44.692 --> 40:47.319
-[man 1] Hey!
-[man 2] They're dogs! Wild dogs!

40:47.820 --> 40:50.364
-No! No!
-[barking]

40:50.448 --> 40:52.700
-[snarls]
-[barking]

40:52.783 --> 40:54.243
-Get away from us.
-[man 1] Get back!

40:54.326 --> 40:57.246
[barking and growling]

40:59.457 --> 41:01.375
[men shouting indistinctly]

41:03.752 --> 41:06.130
Throw the boy to them. Feed the dogs!

41:08.382 --> 41:11.093
-No, don't! You can't! You can't!
-Hey!

41:12.219 --> 41:14.180
[both scream]

41:16.265 --> 41:19.477
-[child Ka-young] Hunbish! No!
-[growling]

41:22.980 --> 41:23.856
[gasping]

41:24.482 --> 41:25.900
-[whimpers]
-[man 2] Let's go, now!

41:25.983 --> 41:28.110
-[cries]
-While the dogs feast,

41:28.194 --> 41:29.361
we can escape and live.

41:32.114 --> 41:33.449
[growling]

41:33.532 --> 41:36.869
-[gasping, screaming]
-[man 2] Go! Go! Let's go!

41:39.788 --> 41:41.457
[Hunbish screams]

41:42.041 --> 41:44.168
The time has come to grant your wishes.

41:45.836 --> 41:46.754
[chuckles softly]

41:47.379 --> 41:49.465
-[child Ka-young cries, yelps]
-[Hunbish screaming]

41:51.467 --> 41:53.093
-[grunts]
-[yelps]

41:53.177 --> 41:55.012
[screaming]

41:55.095 --> 41:56.180
[man 2] Don't look.

41:56.263 --> 41:58.098
[soft chiming]

42:02.353 --> 42:04.230
[gusting]

42:04.313 --> 42:05.439
[man 3] Iblis is here!

42:05.523 --> 42:07.525
-[man 4] Oh, God! [yelps]
-[man 3] It's Satan!

42:07.608 --> 42:09.693
-[men screaming]
-[man 4] Oh, God!

42:11.195 --> 42:13.614
Stop! Throw the girl! Throw her too!

42:13.697 --> 42:16.617
[man 2] Let's go now! Hurry! Come on!

42:16.700 --> 42:19.119
-Gather everything and go!
-[man 4] Leave her! Let's go!

42:19.203 --> 42:21.372
-[rumbling]
-[men screaming]

42:22.831 --> 42:24.458
Hurry! Keep moving!

42:24.542 --> 42:26.961
[hopeful music playing]

42:35.261 --> 42:36.345
[gasping]

42:38.138 --> 42:40.349
[echoing] I am a genie,
a spirit of the lamp.

42:41.058 --> 42:44.228
I'll grant you three wishes. Make them.

42:45.396 --> 42:46.647
Wishes?

42:47.523 --> 42:48.399
Really?

42:49.108 --> 42:52.361
No bringing back the dead
or traveling to the future.

42:52.444 --> 42:56.407
Anything other than that, your wish…

42:58.242 --> 42:59.493
is my command.

43:01.787 --> 43:03.038
Where are you from?

43:03.122 --> 43:05.291
[gasps] Are you from Goryeo too?

43:08.419 --> 43:11.255
If that would bring you comfort,
let's say I am.

43:11.922 --> 43:13.549
Now make your first wish.

43:13.632 --> 43:16.010
-[Hunbish screaming]
-[dogs growling]

43:18.429 --> 43:20.806
Would you please save Hunbish
from the wolves?

43:21.307 --> 43:23.684
Oh, please!
Let him live a long, long life!

43:24.518 --> 43:27.646
Please let him live!
He can't die like this!

43:28.397 --> 43:29.565
That's right.

43:32.943 --> 43:34.069
Follow me…

43:35.321 --> 43:36.530
to your corruption.

43:41.243 --> 43:42.494
-[gasps]
-[chiming]

43:45.539 --> 43:47.249
[screaming]

43:48.667 --> 43:51.295
[wind gusting]

43:54.423 --> 43:55.341
[screaming stops]

43:57.092 --> 43:58.594
[rumbling]

44:01.180 --> 44:02.598
-[blood splatters]
-[groans]

44:04.683 --> 44:05.934
[man 1] Satan's found us!

44:07.353 --> 44:09.980
-[Iblis] Don't blame me.
-[man 2] Run! Satan's gonna kill us!

44:10.064 --> 44:14.026
[Iblis] My young master has wished
for someone to live a long life.

44:14.109 --> 44:15.694
[rumbling]

44:17.112 --> 44:18.822
[flesh squelching]

44:21.992 --> 44:27.289
A long, lengthy life
is bound to require blood sacrifices.

44:30.250 --> 44:33.712
This blood will taint the desert.

44:33.796 --> 44:36.882
[dramatic orchestral music plays]

44:36.965 --> 44:38.425
The boy will live,

44:39.259 --> 44:41.387
but the pack of wild dogs will starve.

44:41.470 --> 44:43.305
[music intensifies]

44:50.020 --> 44:51.897
[breathes heavily]

44:51.980 --> 44:52.815
[music fades]

44:58.237 --> 45:00.739
Shall we hear what your second wish is?

45:00.823 --> 45:02.366
[gasping]

45:04.618 --> 45:06.578
Will you make it so that…

45:08.122 --> 45:13.001
children won't be sold
to be fed to animals like I was?

45:16.255 --> 45:17.881
I shall block the path that brought you.

45:19.925 --> 45:21.051
I'll return soon.

45:22.636 --> 45:24.596
[dramatic music plays]

45:27.266 --> 45:29.268
[birds cawing]

45:38.235 --> 45:39.069
[music stops]

45:39.153 --> 45:41.655
This is around 1041 AD.

45:43.407 --> 45:45.492
You're sure it was the year 1041?

45:46.452 --> 45:47.286
I'm sure.

45:48.203 --> 45:52.416
This period was when he was at his peak
of corrupting humans. [inhales sharply]

45:53.292 --> 45:55.919
There was a very large
number of deaths that year.

45:57.045 --> 45:57.880
Including yours.

46:00.757 --> 46:02.384
[birds cawing]

46:02.968 --> 46:05.429
That's his handiwork, all those deaths.

46:07.598 --> 46:09.349
All that blood on Iblis' hands.

46:14.646 --> 46:16.315
[groans, pants]

46:21.320 --> 46:22.738
[growling]

46:23.864 --> 46:26.074
-[child Ka-young gasps]
-[dogs barking]

46:28.118 --> 46:30.787
[Sade growling]

46:30.871 --> 46:32.789
[child Ka-young gasping]

46:35.918 --> 46:36.877
Oh, they're there.

46:37.628 --> 46:39.338
You see me standing with the scythe?

46:41.507 --> 46:43.926
I haven't seen my original face
in a long time.

46:44.760 --> 46:45.886
I'll change it,

46:45.969 --> 46:47.763
so it's easier to recognize.
[snaps fingers]

46:54.520 --> 46:56.605
Your second wish has also been fulfilled.

46:57.356 --> 46:59.566
The path between the desert
and Goryeo has been blocked.

47:00.192 --> 47:01.860
Because of tsunamis and earthquakes.

47:03.153 --> 47:05.989
Your first wish caused
the death of 15 merchants.

47:06.615 --> 47:09.535
And your second wish
ended hundreds of lives.

47:13.497 --> 47:16.833
I didn't want that.
I didn't make those kinds of wishes.

47:16.917 --> 47:19.294
[man panting] Please, help us--

47:19.795 --> 47:20.629
[man grunts]

47:22.381 --> 47:25.300
Mm. The number has increased to 16.

47:34.643 --> 47:37.104
[Iblis] Now, you have
your final wish remaining.

47:37.688 --> 47:39.773
Girl from Goryeo, make it.

47:42.818 --> 47:46.488
I didn't mean to hurt anyone.
Please, what can I do to fix this?

47:48.615 --> 47:53.161
I didn't mean-- [sobbing]
I made the wrong kinds of wishes.

47:55.455 --> 47:56.623
Foolish child.

47:57.374 --> 47:59.835
Do you truly believe
there's a right kind of wish?

48:00.544 --> 48:03.297
To gain something, one has to lose.

48:03.380 --> 48:06.091
For one to live, someone's life
must come to an end.

48:07.217 --> 48:08.135
Sade!

48:08.802 --> 48:10.679
[growling]

48:14.349 --> 48:16.685
-[whimpers]
-[dogs growling]

48:17.936 --> 48:20.105
-[barking]
-[screaming]

48:24.610 --> 48:25.986
[child Ka-young screams]

48:26.069 --> 48:27.362
-[whistles]
-[dog barks]

48:30.115 --> 48:31.491
[child Ka-young panting]

48:34.494 --> 48:37.789
No matter what you say, I know
your last wish will be to save yourself.

48:37.873 --> 48:39.958
-[breath shuddering]
-Now make it.

48:48.592 --> 48:49.635
[child Ka-young] No.

48:51.261 --> 48:52.387
I accept…

48:54.056 --> 48:55.140
punishment.

48:56.767 --> 48:58.518
So… [pants]

48:59.144 --> 49:00.145
make sure…

49:02.105 --> 49:04.024
we are punished right…

49:05.400 --> 49:08.111
you and me, please.

49:11.406 --> 49:12.240
What?

49:12.783 --> 49:14.826
This is the only way it's fair.

49:14.910 --> 49:16.203
[breathes laboriously]

49:16.286 --> 49:17.329
That's my…

49:18.413 --> 49:20.290
That's my final wish.

49:20.374 --> 49:22.709
[tense music playing]

49:28.965 --> 49:29.800
[huffs]

49:30.967 --> 49:32.469
You petty little human…

49:34.805 --> 49:37.516
How dare you do this,
you pathetic lump of clay!

49:37.599 --> 49:40.268
[breathing heavily]

49:41.645 --> 49:43.063
[Ejllael laughs]

49:43.647 --> 49:47.734
Behold. His creations do know
right from wrong. They're righteous.

49:47.818 --> 49:48.944
You've lost, Iblis.

49:50.237 --> 49:51.571
You remember what He said?

49:52.072 --> 49:55.158
If you meet even one human who's pure,
you will be trapped.

49:55.242 --> 49:56.868
-Wait, just wait.
-For eternity!

49:56.952 --> 49:58.412
You need to wait and hear me out!

50:01.123 --> 50:02.416
Ri-- Righteous?

50:03.166 --> 50:05.711
[scoffs] Really? There's…

50:06.628 --> 50:10.465
[pants] Well, there's always…
there's room for interpretation.

50:12.467 --> 50:14.428
Please put in a good word,
won't you? Brother?

50:15.887 --> 50:16.722
[scoffs]

50:19.933 --> 50:20.809
Cut the bullshit.

50:20.892 --> 50:22.436
[gasps softly]

50:22.519 --> 50:23.854
[laughs]

50:28.900 --> 50:30.152
Is this really the end?

50:31.194 --> 50:32.070
Because of her?

50:33.780 --> 50:34.823
We need to talk.

50:35.407 --> 50:38.034
Ejllael. You need to come back!

50:38.869 --> 50:41.079
[breathing heavily]

50:42.622 --> 50:44.750
[tense orchestral music plays]

50:47.085 --> 50:48.462
You small lump of clay.

50:49.463 --> 50:51.548
You lowly being created on Friday.

50:51.631 --> 50:53.925
A mere human
who doesn't live past a hundred years!

51:01.016 --> 51:03.226
[tense orchestral music continues]

51:11.943 --> 51:13.361
[deep rumbling]

51:20.368 --> 51:23.079
[breathes heavily]

51:28.418 --> 51:29.252
[music fades]

51:38.887 --> 51:40.889
[wistful music playing]

52:02.160 --> 52:03.245
[Ejllael] Hmm.

52:04.037 --> 52:06.832
Do you see?
You died in this way so tragically.

52:08.124 --> 52:10.085
No matter what you wished for,

52:10.168 --> 52:12.754
Iblis always heard it the way
he wanted to hear it,

52:12.838 --> 52:14.172
to lead you to corruption.

52:20.095 --> 52:22.097
[wistful music continues]

52:30.313 --> 52:31.648
I thought I saw…

52:33.275 --> 52:34.192
rage.

52:34.943 --> 52:37.070
[suspenseful music plays]

52:37.153 --> 52:41.449
When I saw it in the lamp,
it looked like rage to me.

52:42.742 --> 52:43.743
This is…

52:46.121 --> 52:47.122
the face…

52:50.667 --> 52:51.668
of remorse.

52:53.086 --> 52:54.212
True sorrow.

52:56.756 --> 52:58.049
[sighs softly]

53:06.641 --> 53:07.976
[Iblis inhales sharply]

53:17.652 --> 53:19.487
[chiming]

53:20.196 --> 53:22.198
[suspenseful music intensifies]

53:29.164 --> 53:31.082
[strained grunting]

53:36.254 --> 53:37.923
[gasping]

53:39.674 --> 53:40.634
How funny it is.

53:40.717 --> 53:42.010
[panting]

53:42.093 --> 53:43.094
[screams]

53:43.178 --> 53:46.848
A mere thousand years
is nothing relative to eternity.

53:46.932 --> 53:48.183
A drop in the bucket.

53:48.808 --> 53:50.060
[sizzling]

53:52.228 --> 53:54.856
[dramatic choral music plays]

53:54.940 --> 53:56.775
[groaning, gasping]

53:59.361 --> 54:00.904
[strained groaning]

54:05.742 --> 54:07.494
[gasping]

54:08.662 --> 54:10.497
-[music stops]
-[gasps deeply]

54:11.873 --> 54:13.875
[gentle music plays]
